          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زبردستی — zabardastī — \"force (making someone do something)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اگر وہ نہیں چاہتا تو زبردستی ٹھیک نہیں۔ agar voh nahīṅ chāhtā to zabardastī ṭhīk nahīṅ. If he doesn't want to, forcing him isn't right."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زبردستی (zabardastī) is built on zabardast, \"having the upper hand\", usually traced to Persian zabardast, from zabar, \"above\", and dast, \"a hand\", with the noun ending -ī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
